\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let X be uniform on ${-1,1}^n$, $u:{-1,1}^n\to [-1,1]$, and $Y\in {-1,1}$ have conditional mean u(X). If $T_\rho $ independently flips cube coordinates with correlation $\rho $, must $I(T_\rho u)\leq \psi (|\rho |\psi ^{-1}(I(u)))$ for all $-1\leq \rho \leq 1$, where $I(u)=h(Eu)-E$ h(u), h(a) is the binary entropy of (1+a)/2, and $\psi (a)=\log $ $2-h(a)$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let X be uniform on ${-1,1}^n$, $u:{-1,1}^n\to [-1,1]$, and $Y\in {-1,1}$ have conditional mean u(X). If $T_\rho $ independently flips cube coordinates with correlation $\rho $, must $I(T_\rho u)\leq \psi (|\rho |\psi ^{-1}(I(u)))$ for all $-1\leq \rho \leq 1$, where $I(u)=h(Eu)-E$ h(u), h(a) is the binary entropy of (1+a)/2, and $\psi (a)=\log $ $2-h(a)$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Sharp-binary-information-contraction-on-the-discrete-cube-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

