\section*{Sharp binary-channel information contraction on the cube}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 119; 2026-09-24), the asserted result is that among binary summaries with fixed information on a uniform cube, a noisy coordinate retains the most information, including the Courtade--Kumar bound and a bias-sensitive refinement.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 119; 2026-09-24), a three-point configuration optimizes the local join. Separate entropy budgets and a reserve for thinning either common output close the dimension induction; integration of the mean-dependent entropy-production bound along the noise semigroup gives the sharp contraction.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 119; 2026-09-24).

\subsection{Formal verification}
For manuscript 1 (family 119; 2026-09-24), OpenAI lists Lean statements for this assertion: among binary summaries with fixed information on a uniform cube, a noisy coordinate retains the most information, including the Courtade--Kumar bound and a bias-sensitive refinement.

The selected statement includes the clause used for this problem.

The linked family Comparator checks are \texttt{CourtadeKumar.lean}, \texttt{SoftChannel204.lean}.

Their named declarations include \texttt{OAI.LeanBlast.CourtadeKumar.courtadeKumarAndAttainment}, \texttt{OAI.SoftChannel204.fullMain}.

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

